{%- liquid
  assign logo_height = settings.logo_height | default: 64

  # The header's own picker wins; the theme-level Brand logo is the fallback so
  # a merchant who sets it once in Theme settings sees it here.
  assign logo_source = section.settings.logo | default: settings.logo

  assign has_feature = false
  if section.settings.feature_label != blank and section.settings.feature_link != blank
    assign has_feature = true
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Two rows on a wide screen: the mark and the one standing invitation on the
  first, the menu and the shop actions on the second. That is what lets the
  navigation start at the inline edge rather than being squeezed between a logo
  and a row of icons.

  It is one grid, not two markup rows — on a narrow screen the same three
  elements collapse into a single line, so nothing is duplicated and nothing
  has to be hidden twice.
{%- endcomment -%}
<header class="header">
  <div class="container container--ultra header__inner">
    <a class="header__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">
      {%- comment -%}
        width/height reserve the box before the file arrives, so they have to
        describe the real artwork: the uploaded image's own dimensions, or the
        bundled SVG's 59.014 x 47.775 viewBox scaled to the default 64px height.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if logo_source -%}
        <img
          class="header__logo-image"
          src="{{ logo_source | image_url: width: 400 }}"
          alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
          style="block-size: {{ logo_height }}px;"
          width="{{ logo_source.width }}"
          height="{{ logo_source.height }}">
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          class="header__logo-image"
          src="{{ 'logo-black.svg' | asset_url }}"
          alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
          style="block-size: {{ logo_height }}px;"
          width="79"
          height="64">
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    {%- if has_feature -%}
      <p class="header__feature">
        <a class="anchor-arrow header__feature-link" href="{{ section.settings.feature_link }}">
          {{ section.settings.feature_label }}
          {%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right' -%}
        </a>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <nav class="header__nav" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.primary_navigation' | t }}">
      <ul class="header__menu" role="list">
        {%- for link in section.settings.menu.links -%}
          <li class="header__item">
            {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A nested menu is a <details> disclosure, like the mobile one:
                it opens, closes and takes focus with no script at all. The
                parent's own destination stays reachable as the first item of
                the panel, so nesting a link never buries it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <details class="header__disclosure">
                <summary class="header__link header__link--parent{% if link.active %} is-active{% endif %}">
                  {{ link.title }}
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-down' -%}
                </summary>
                <ul class="header__panel" role="list">
                  <li>
                    <a
                      class="header__panel-link"
                      href="{{ link.url }}"
                      {%- if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                      {{ link.title }}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                  {%- for child in link.links -%}
                    <li>
                      <a
                        class="header__panel-link{% if child.active %} is-active{% endif %}"
                        href="{{ child.url }}"
                        {%- if child.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                        {{ child.title }}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </details>
            {%- else -%}
              <a
                class="header__link{% if link.active %} is-active{% endif %}"
                href="{{ link.url }}"
                {%- if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                {{ link.title }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="header__actions">
      <a class="header__action" href="{{ routes.search_url }}">
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'search' -%}
        <span class="header__action-label">{{ 'general.search.title' | t }}</span>
      </a>

      {%- comment -%}
        A link, not a button: with scripting off it navigates to /cart. The
        drawer component upgrades it to open the drawer instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="header__action" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" data-cart-link>
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'cart' -%}
        <span class="header__action-label">{{ 'cart.general.title' | t }}</span>
        {%- comment -%}
          Two counts, two hooks. The badge is decorative (aria-hidden); the
          visually-hidden sentence is what a screen reader announces. Both are
          refreshed by syncCartCount after an ajax cart change; syncing only the
          badge leaves the announced total stale.

          The sentence is a polite live region, so an ajax change is heard and
          not only seen. aria-atomic reads the whole sentence rather than the
          digit that changed, which on its own would announce "2" and nothing
          else. It matters most on the cart page, where a quantity change
          updates this count and opens no drawer to announce itself.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="header__cart-count" aria-hidden="true" data-cart-count>{{ cart.item_count | default: 0 }}</span>
        <span
          class="visually-hidden"
          aria-live="polite"
          aria-atomic="true"
          data-cart-count-label>{{ cart.item_count | default: 0 }} {{ 'general.accessibility.cart_count' | t }}</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      A <details> disclosure rather than a scripted toggle, so the menu opens
      even if theme.js never loads.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <details class="header__mobile">
      {%- comment -%}
        Both icons and both names are in the markup, and CSS shows the pair that
        matches [open]. The alternative — swapping them in script — would leave
        the toggle stuck on "Menu" in exactly the case this disclosure exists
        for, a page whose JavaScript never ran. <summary> supplies aria-expanded
        on its own; this is the same state drawn for the people reading it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <summary class="header__action header__mobile-toggle">
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'menu' -%}
        {%- render 'icon', name: 'close' -%}
        <span class="visually-hidden header__mobile-name--open">{{ 'general.accessibility.menu' | t }}</span>
        <span class="visually-hidden header__mobile-name--close">{{ 'general.accessibility.close_menu' | t }}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="header__mobile-panel">
        <ul class="header__mobile-menu" role="list">
          {%- for link in section.settings.menu.links -%}
            <li>
              <a class="header__mobile-link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a>
              {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
                <ul class="header__mobile-sub" role="list">
                  {%- for child in link.links -%}
                    <li><a class="header__mobile-sublink" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a></li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The standing invitation, and on a phone this is the only place it
            appears. Drawn as a button rather than as a seventh navigation link,
            so it keeps the weight it has in the desktop header instead of
            disappearing into the list it closes.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if has_feature -%}
            <li class="header__mobile-feature">
              <a class="button" href="{{ section.settings.feature_link }}">{{ section.settings.feature_label }}</a>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</header>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Header",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "logo",
      "label": "Logo",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the bundled vector logo. Never display the full lockup below 57 px tall."
    },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu", "label": "Menu", "default": "main-menu" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "feature_label",
      "label": "Standing invitation",
      "default": "Request a Sample",
      "info": "The one link that sits beside the logo. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "feature_link",
      "label": "Standing invitation link",
      "default": "/pages/request-a-sample"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Header" }]
}
{% endschema %}
